      "message": "The test flow does not match the test name and documentation.\nAlthough the test is named `Change User Privilege When LDAP Unreachable` and describes a privilege change involving an LDAP user, `LDAP_Admin` is only used to create `test_local_user`. After LDAP becomes unreachable, the test switches back to the local admin and performs the `PATCH` to change the user\u0027s `RoleId`. The LDAP user is therefore never actually used for the privilege change.\n\nIf the intent is only to verify that the local admin can still modify user information when LDAP is unreachable while the LDAP user cannot log in, the existing test already covers this scenario. In that case, this commit appears to provide overlapping coverage.",
